      "role": "user",
      "content": "so it's not just my imagination then? i thought i was losing it hearing actual \"beats\" in the signal. \n\nif that's what it is, i was able to catch a much longer sequence when the backup started running. it wasn't just random, it sounded way more organized, almost like a sequence of commands. it went: long-short-short, long-long-short, then a really fast jittery burst. \n\nif you apply that BOR theory, do you think that specific rhythm could represent a handshake or maybe a specific type of encryption protocol being negotiated? it felt very intentional.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
